@startuml
title 01  |  Catalog evidence refresh

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #37678C
  LifeLineBorderColor #A9BAC8
  ParticipantBorderColor #476782
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF3FA
  ActorBorderColor #476782
  ActorBackgroundColor #EAF3FA
  GroupBorderColor #91AAC0
  GroupBackgroundColor #F5F9FC
  NoteBorderColor #D7B766
  NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E7
}

actor Operator
boundary "Streamlit UI" as UI
control "Refresh controller" as Controller
control "Catalog service" as Catalog
entity "Approved source adapter" as Source
database "SQLite repository" as Store

Operator -> UI: Click Refresh product for known variant
UI -> Controller: Pass stable public product ID only
Controller -> Store: Read enabled source, exact reviewed mapping,
and current catalog
Store --> Controller: Approved source and current mapped variant
alt Source/mapping unavailable or ambiguous
  Controller --> UI: Read-only catalog and recovery guidance
else Authorized target
  Controller -> Source: Lookup mapped barcode (bounded attempts/cache)
  Source --> Controller: Validated candidates and payload-free outcome
  Controller -> Store: Revalidate source and mapping; commit atomically
  alt Valid mapped candidates
    Store --> Controller: Append unverified evidence + outcome
(or unchanged replay)
  else Missing/failed source result
    Store --> Controller: Store safe failure outcome; preserve facts
  else Changed variant or storage failure
    Store --> Controller: Reject write; prior catalog retained
  end
  Controller -> Catalog: Read current facts and evaluate evidence policy
  Catalog --> Controller: Selected values, dates, freshness, conflicts
  Controller --> UI: Source outcome + separate storage status
  UI --> Operator: Show actual dates, validation, and recovery guidance
end

note over UI, Store
  No automatic fetch, arbitrary URL, or private search input.
  Existing selections stay unchanged; refresh candidates remain unverified.
  Unsaved attempts are session-only; stored outcomes survive restart.
end note
@enduml
